# ================================================================== headers
@App_FrontEndStateMachine Main application state machine (front end, demo, game).
@App_FrontEndStateMachine State in B_2831e: 0 = boot (Atari intro, logos, title),
@App_FrontEndStateMachine 1 = logos + title again (after the demo), 2 = front end menus,
@App_FrontEndStateMachine 3 = demo mode, 4 = quit.

@Round_Run Plays one round: sets up the level, then loops until the round ends.
@Round_Run Local state machine on gRoundState (see Round_UpdateLogic); each loop
@Round_Run iteration updates the logic, draws a frame and waits for the screen swap.
@Round_Run gGameMode: 0 = 4-player battle, 1 = team battle, 2 = puzzle,
@Round_Run 3 = stage challenge. gLevelSet: 0-3 = puzzle worlds, 4 = stage
@Round_Run challenge, 5 = battle levels.

@Round_UpdateLogic One frame of game logic, dispatched on gRoundState:
@Round_UpdateLogic   state 4 = normal play: age arrows, move cats, move mice,
@Round_UpdateLogic             spawn creatures, update players (input/AI/arrows),
@Round_UpdateLogic             game clock, AI path maps, spinner event timer
@Round_UpdateLogic   state 2/3  = puzzle running / puzzle fast forward
@Round_UpdateLogic   state 6    = spinner roulette (Spinner_Spin)
@Round_UpdateLogic   state 9    = demo: go to the next level (0-24, wraps)

@Round_SetState in: d0 = new round state. Entering state 4 (play) records the
@Round_SetState frame clock in gRoundStartClock.

@Level_GetCell in: d0 = row (0-8), d1 = column (0-11). out: a0 = cell (2 bytes)
@Level_GetCell in the current level map: map + $22 + row*24 + column*2.
@Level_GetCell Cell byte 0: bits 0-3 = walls, bits 4-6 = type
@Level_GetCell   ($00 empty, $10 spawner, $20 rocket, $30 hole, $40 arrow).
@Level_GetCell Cell byte 1: bits 0-1 = arrow direction (0 left, 1 right, 2 down, 3 up).

@Level_GetArrowStock Puzzle mode: number of arrows of direction d0 available in the
@Level_GetArrowStock level (level header bytes $1e-$21, one per direction).

@Creature_Move Moves one creature (mouse or cat) by d0 (16.16 fixed point, in tiles).
@Creature_Move in: a0 = creature, d0 = distance for this frame.
@Creature_Move Creature record (26 bytes):
@Creature_Move   +$00.l x   (high word = column 0-11, low word $8000 = tile centre)
@Creature_Move   +$04.l y   (high word = row 0-8)
@Creature_Move   +$08.l animation counter
@Creature_Move   +$10.w direction (0 left, 1 right, 2 down, 3 up)
@Creature_Move   +$12.w kind (1 mouse, 2 gold mouse, 3 purple mouse, 4 cat)
@Creature_Move   +$14.w state (0 free slot, 1 walking, 2 falling into a hole,
@Creature_Move          3 caught / flying, 5 entering a rocket)
@Creature_Move   +$16.w "state just changed" flag
@Creature_Move Algorithm:
@Creature_Move   if the current tile is a rocket: state = 5, Rocket_Enter()
@Creature_Move   if the current tile is a hole:   state = 2 (falls)
@Creature_Move   while distance left:
@Creature_Move     advance along the direction; the board wraps around (12 x 9)
@Creature_Move     when crossing the centre of a tile:
@Creature_Move       index = (arrow ? arrow direction : direction) * 16 + walls
@Creature_Move       new direction = gTurnTable[index]   ("turn right at walls")
@Creature_Move       a cat meeting an arrow that points against it damages the
@Creature_Move       arrow (Arrow_HitByCat)
@Creature_Move       on a turn: snap to the centre, keep the remaining distance

@Mice_Update Moves every mouse (up to 128, gMice, active bits in gMiceActiveMask).
@Mice_Update Speed = MouseSpeeds[1], or [0]/[2] during the Slow Down / Speed Up
@Mice_Update spinner events; puzzle fast forward uses [2]. During Mouse Monopoly
@Mice_Update the mice fly straight to the rocket of the spinner player.
@Mice_Update A mouse that touches a cat (Mouse_TouchesCat) is caught (state 3);
@Mice_Update a mouse that fell or was caught is removed after 8 animation frames.

@Mouse_Spawn in: d0 = row, d1 = column, d2 = direction, kind and flight slot on
@Mouse_Spawn the stack. Takes the first free slot of gMice.

@Mouse_TouchesCat in: a0 = mouse. out: d0 = 1 if a cat in the same tile is closer
@Mouse_TouchesCat than the catch distance on both axes.

@Cats_Update Moves every cat (up to 32, gCats). Same speed rules as the mice with
@Cats_Update CatSpeeds (cats are slower). Also rebuilds gCatOccupancy, a per-tile
@Cats_Update bit mask of the cats standing in or next to each tile (collisions).

@Spawners_Update Spawns mice and cats from the spawner tiles ($10) of the level.
@Spawners_Update The spawn mode depends on the spinner event (Mouse Mania, Cat Mania...)
@Spawners_Update and on the stage challenge objective.

@Arrows_Age Battle, team and challenge modes: every arrow loses one frame of life
@Arrows_Age per frame (arrow cell +$18) and is removed when it reaches zero.
@Arrows_Age Arrow cell record (26 bytes, gArrowCells[9][12]):
@Arrows_Age   +$00.w column, +$04.w row, +$10.w direction, +$12.w owner player,
@Arrows_Age   +$14.w health (0 none, 2 new, 1 damaged once), +$18.w frames left
@Arrows_Age   (the arrow blinks when fewer than 75 frames are left).

@Arrow_Remove in: d0 = row, d1 = column. Removes the arrow, updates the owner's
@Arrow_Remove arrow count and the arrow row mask.

@Arrow_HitByCat A cat walked into an arrow pointing against it: a new arrow
@Arrow_HitByCat becomes damaged, a damaged arrow is removed (two hits).

@Arrow_Create in: d0 = row, d1 = column, d2 = direction, owner on the stack.
@Arrow_Create out: a0 = arrow cell, or 0 if the tile holds an arrow, a hole,
@Arrow_Create a spawner or a rocket.

@Player_PlaceArrow in: a0 = player, d0 = row, d1 = column, d2 = direction.
@Player_PlaceArrow Puzzle: clicking an arrow removes it, otherwise one arrow of the
@Player_PlaceArrow level stock is placed (error sound when none is left).
@Player_PlaceArrow Other modes: a player owns 3 arrow slots; the new arrow replaces
@Player_PlaceArrow a free slot or the player's oldest arrow.

@Rocket_Enter A creature entered a rocket (a0 = creature):
@Rocket_Enter   mouse        -> owner +1
@Rocket_Enter   gold mouse   -> owner +50
@Rocket_Enter   purple mouse -> owner +1 and the spinner starts (Spinner_Trigger)
@Rocket_Enter   cat          -> the owner loses a third of his score
@Rocket_Enter                   (Player_CatInRocket)

@Player_AddScore in: d0 = player, d1 = points. The score never goes below 0.
@Player_AddScore Player record: 222 bytes at gPlayers (+$46 active, +$48 score,
@Player_AddScore +$52/+$56 cursor x/y, +$5a/+$5e cursor column/row, +$72 controller,
@Player_AddScore 14 = CPU).

@Player_CatInRocket A cat entered the player's rocket: score -= score / 3.

@Players_Update Once per frame for every active player: read the controller
@Players_Update (human) or run the AI (CPU, controller 14), clamp the cursor to the
@Players_Update board, and place an arrow when a direction button is pressed.
@Players_Update Puzzle mode also handles the GO / FFWD / REDO / EXIT buttons.

@Ai_Update One CPU player per call (d0 = player, a0 = cursor). States:
@Ai_Update   0 think: wait for the reaction delay, then look for the best arrow
@Ai_Update            (Ai_FindBestArrow, up to 3 strategies)
@Ai_Update   1 move:  slide the cursor towards the chosen tile
@Ai_Update   2 place: press the direction button for the chosen arrow
@Ai_Update The reaction delay comes from AiReactionFrames plus a random part.

@Ai_FindBestArrow Uses the path maps (Ai_GetFlowMap / Ai_GetRocketMap): for each
@Ai_FindBestArrow empty tile on a creature flow, the arrow direction that sends the flow
@Ai_FindBestArrow to the target rocket by the shortest path. out: d0 = 1 if found,
@Ai_FindBestArrow the tile and direction are stored in the AI record.

@Ai_UpdatePathMaps Recomputes, a piece per frame, the maps of the tiles followed by
@Ai_UpdatePathMaps the creatures and their distances to each rocket (used by the AI).

@Spinner_Trigger A purple mouse entered the rocket of player d0: remember the
@Spinner_Trigger player and switch the round to state 6 (roulette).

@Spinner_Spin Picks a random event (0-7) and applies it:
@Spinner_Spin   0 Cat Attack      1 Cat Mania       2 Everybody Move  3 Mouse Mania
@Spinner_Spin   4 Mouse Monopoly  5 Place Arrows Again  6 Slow Down  7 Speed Up
@Spinner_Spin (same order as the pictures in SPINNER.GFX). Timed events last 500
@Spinner_Spin frames, Mouse Monopoly 150.

@Spinner_TickEvent Counts down the running spinner event and ends it at zero.

@Random in: d0 = n. out: d0 = random number in 0..n-1.
@Random Linear congruential generator: seed = seed * $10dcd + $29 (gRandomSeed).

@Sfx_Play in: d0 = sound, d1 = priority, d2 = stereo pan (see ColumnPan).
@Music_Play in: d1 = tune number.
